I'm now statically importing `codemirror.css` which results in Vite analyzing looking at that at build time and including it in a larger CSS bundle that's loaded for the REPL (rather than having it be its own file like in the current REPL). Including `import './codemirror.js';` in `onMount` didn't help anything, but doing that rather than using a SvelteKit-ism (`import { browser } from '$app/env';` seems nicer (and leaving it as it was was not an option, as we had to do something to prevent that code from ending up in the server bundle). I don't know whether it's a known/expected limitation of Vite to not be able to handle CSS files that are imported on the browser as part of a dynamic `import()`.

The `import marked from 'marked';` makes that part work in the production build, but now the dev build is broken. There are a few ways to fix this, and probably one of them is the PR Ben submitted to `marked` but I believe we would also need the `pkg.exports` map in place as well. Barring waiting for that, I think we could also try to get `marked` bundled into the site build. The reason it isn't being bundled currently is because it's also a production dependency of the site directly (in addition to a dependency of the REPL) and so the Node adapter tells esbuild to mark it as external. I haven't looked into whether moving that to a dev dependency would just work. I assume there was some reason it was external before, perhaps just that Rollup at the time didn't like bundling it for some reason.

